RUNS      2, identical

WHAT IT PINS
  The entry Thread's index is 1. That is the reference's `Table` policy showing through: `array`
  starts as `[None]`, so index 0 is reserved and the first allocation is 1. `switch.reading` records
  the same 1 for its ASYNC lift, so the number is not an artefact of either lift shape.

WHAT IT DOES NOT PIN
  The slot-reuse ORDER. One Thread exists here, so nothing is ever freed and no policy is
  discriminated — see switch.reading's note, which cannot discriminate it either for a different
  reason (exactly one slot free at each creation). A fixture holding two Threads live and freeing
  them out of order would.

  Execution order. Not applicable: one Thread.

GATE OFF (wasmtime)
  `thread.index` requires the component model threading feature (at offset 0xb)
  exit 1 — a parse refusal naming the production

